From dc5a48007376098dcccfcf12a50048d2b774d4b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:38:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/14] PlaitOS: settings for the PlaitOS features

Rows for every PlaitOS framework option, in two homes
(design: plait-os docs/plait-settings-layout.md):

- Slotted into the stock page that already holds the related setting:
  Press & hold power button (torch with screen off and its auto-off timer,
  advanced restart, power menu entries), Gestures (double-tap to sleep),
  3-button navigation (long-press home, back and recents actions),
  Lock screen (Peek Display, always-on schedule with from/till times, AOD
  while charging, pocket mode), Display (Smart Pixels), Notifications
  (pop-up duration, force stop in the notification menu), Sound (volume panel
  on the left, panel timeout). Each block is appended under a PlaitOS
  category; stock rows are unchanged
- A PlaitOS page on the home screen for the rest, laid out like crDroid's
  settings: swipeable tabs (Status bar, Quick Settings, Buttons, Misc), sub-
  screens for network speed and the Quick Settings grid, and "Reset PlaitOS
  settings" in the menu

Rows are keyed by the setting they write; PlaitSettings knows each key's
table (System/Secure/Global) and default, so one generic switch and one list
controller serve almost every row. Special cases: power menu entries
(multi-select, power and restart always kept), the AOD schedule times (time
pickers, shown only for the modes that use them), Peek Display (also turns on
the stock "Wake screen for notifications") and main-user-only rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
